**© 2026 Belona Cybersecurity LLC.** All rights reserved.
Powder Springs, Georgia, United States · belonacyber.com · contact@belonacyber.com

This repository contains the technical portfolio of Belona Cybersecurity LLC: the
documentation of security engineering work performed by the company, authored by
the company, and published by the company. It is **not** open-source material and
it is **not** a template.

## What you may do

You may read, download and print these documents, and share links to this
repository, for the purpose of evaluating Belona Cybersecurity LLC as a service
provider, a vendor or an employer. You may quote short excerpts for commentary or
review, provided the company is credited by name.

## What requires written permission

Everything else, including:

- republishing these documents, in whole or in part, anywhere else;
- presenting this work, or any part of it, as your own or as your
  organization's;
- removing or altering the authorship, copyright or contact information;
- using these documents as a template, model or deliverable for a third party;
- training a machine-learning model on this material.

Requests go to **contact@belonacyber.com**.

## On the anonymization

The engagements documented here are real and were performed under authorization
from the system owner. Client names and infrastructure identifiers were replaced
with placeholders before publication. Belona Cybersecurity LLC does not publish
identifiable client data without written authorization.

## Authorship of record

The authoritative record of authorship is the commit history of this repository,
published under the `belona-cybersecurity` GitHub organization. Each document
carries the company's name in its header and footer, and each PDF carries it in
its document metadata.

